  "evidence": "TEXT_G: £8bn extra for the NHS, mental health parity and £500m uplift, carers’ bonus and new rights, cap care costs, integrate health and social care; expand free childcare, protect disability benefits, Living Wage in central government, transparency to close the gender pay gap; protect the Human Rights Act, champion LGBT+ equality, fair asylum and welcoming skilled migrants/students; clamp down on tax avoidance and non‑dom status, levy on high‑value property; affordable housing, tenant protections, cleaner air and public‑health measures (junk‑food marketing curbs, minimum alcohol pricing). TEXT_D: Leave the EU and end free movement, five‑year moratorium on unskilled immigration, prefer British workers, revoke citizenship for terrorists; restrict full benefits and most NHS access to five years’ contributions, end health tourism; £12bn for the NHS, £1.5bn for mental health, more GPs/nurses; leave the ECHR and enact a UK Bill of Rights, +6,000 police/prison/Border posts; cut overseas aid, repeal the Climate Change Act and end green levies.",
